condition_name: Giardiasis
condition_slug: giardiasis
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: A parasitic protozoal infection caused by Giardia lamblia or Giardia intestinalis. Worldwide in distribution but more common in developing countries. Spread is by the faeco-oral route.
clinical_features[2]:
  - type: Acute disease
    features[1]: watery diarrhoea with abdominal bloating
  - type: Chronic disease
    features[6]: diarrhoea,steatorrhoea,weight loss from malabsorption syndrome,lactose intolerance,xylose malabsorption,vitamin B deficiency
investigations[3]: Stool microscopy,Full blood count,Duodenal aspirate for microscopy
treatment:
  goals[3]: Eradicate parasite,Correct fluid and electrolyte deficits,Replace malabsorbed nutrients
  non_drug[0]:
  drug[2]: "Metronidazole (Adult: 2 g orally daily for 3 days; or 400 mg 8 hourly for 5 days; or 500 mg twelve hourly for 7 - 10 days; Child 1-3 years: 500 mg orally daily; 3-7 years: 600-800 mg daily; 7-10 years: 1 g daily for 3 days)","Tinidazole (Adult: 40 mg/kg orally as a single dose; or 2 g stat, repeat after 1 week, once if necessary; Child: 50 to 75 mg/kg as a single dose, repeat after 1 week)"
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[0]:
  supportive_measures[2]: Vitamin B supplementation,Correct fluid and electrolyte deficits
differential_diagnoses[0]:
complications[1]: Diseases related to Vitamin B deficiency
prevention[2]: Good Communal and Personal hygiene,Potable water.
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment: null
prognosis: null